@talks halloran-emeka
// TW1, the Talk a while pack: Emeka Halloran's own talks (he/him). Works systems officer; warm and unhurried; laughs
// before the punchline; "lovely"; asks if you've eaten; a terrible joke every breakfast (never at anyone's expense).
// Never says no (his thread); not the mug-giving itself (that's the Day 5 meeting).

== joke
topic: day
them: Want this morning's joke? You've no choice, really. Here it is.
them: What do you call a spanner that tells jokes? A wrench-ed comedian. Ha! I know. I know.   #funny
ask: Go on. Have you got one? Everyone's got one.
listen: Where do you find them?
  them: I make them up in the lift. That's why they're so bad. It's a short lift.   #funny
share: One from home. It's worse than yours.
  them: Lovely! Nothing's worse than mine. Tell it at breakfast. I'll laugh first.   #warm
cheer: That was my joke. You stole it.
  them: Ha! Then we're both guilty. Lovely. Partners in crime.   #funny

== oven-visa
topic: food
when: tier>=acquaintance
them: Brennan let me bake on my rest day. One oven. Supervised. I need a visa for that galley.   #funny
them: Scones, this week. She took one bite and said "Hm." I've been floating since.
ask: Have you eaten? Properly, I mean. Not a biscuit standing up.
listen: Is "Hm." good, from Brennan?
  them: From Brennan, "Hm." is a medal. "Lovely" is the cup. I'll get there.   #funny
share: Not properly. It's been busy.
  them: Ah, no. Grab shelf, then. Go on. I'll walk you. Lovely.   #warm
cheer: A biscuit, standing up. Twice.
  them: Ha! That's two biscuits. Close enough to lunch. Have a scone as well.   #funny

== mug-rack
topic: work
when: tier>=colleague aboard>=5
them: Every mug at the tea corner has a hook. I keep the rack. Somebody has to.
them: The end hook's yours. Always will be. That's how it works. Well. That's how I work it.   #warm
ask: Is there a little job you do that nobody asked you to?
listen: Why do you keep the rack?
  them: Someone kept it when I was new. Never said a word. I just found my mug there.   #warm
share: Wiping down the bench after.
  them: Lovely. That's the Works way. Nobody notices. Everybody's glad.
cheer: Eating the last biscuit. For the team.
  them: Ha! The sacrifice. We all thank you. Quietly.   #funny

== no
topic: plans
when: tier>=friend
them: Can I tell you a funny thing? I've never said no to anyone aboard. Not once.
them: Tea rota, a shift swap, an oven. Yes, yes, yes. I'm a bit tired, honestly. Ha.
ask: Do you find it easy to say no?
listen: What would you say no to, first?
  them: The tea rota. Two years, every week. I'd love one week off it. Ha.
share: Not really. I'm learning.
  them: Then we'll learn together. You say one, I'll say one. Deal?   #warm
cheer: No. See? Easy.
  them: Ha! Show-off. Lovely. I'll practise on you.   #funny
